From: airoha-port <airoha@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: mt7530: accept PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_INTERNAL on switch ports

The AN7583 internal GPHYs are described with phy-mode = "internal" and
mt7988_phy_supported() accepts that mode, but mt753x_phylink_mac_config()
only accepted PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_GMII for ports 0..4 and bailed out via
"goto unsupported"; the following in-band negotiation guard rejected any
non-SGMII interface as well.  Consequently the switch port MAC was never
programmed and lan2/3/4 passed no traffic, logging:

    mt753x_phylink_mac_config: unsupported internal port: 2

Accept the internal interface in both places, matching upstream
mt7988_mac_config(), which simply returns 0 - there is no MII pinout.

Signed-off-by: airoha-port <airoha@local>
---
diff -ruN a/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c b/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c	2026-10-10 07:37:23.210529609 +0800
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c	2026-10-10 07:37:23.210529609 +0800
@@ -2253,7 +2253,14 @@
 	case 2:
 	case 3:
 	case 4:
-		if (state->interface != PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_GMII)
+		/* The AN7583 internal GPHYs are described with
+		 * phy-mode = "internal" in the device tree and
+		 * mt7988_phy_supported() accepts that mode, so accept it here
+		 * too.  Otherwise the port MAC is never programmed and the
+		 * port passes no traffic ("unsupported internal port: N").
+		 */
+		if (state->interface != PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_GMII &&
+		    state->interface != PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_INTERNAL)
 			goto unsupported;
 		break;
 	case 5: /* 2nd cpu port with phy of port 0 or 4 / external phy */
@@ -2284,8 +2291,13 @@
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/* In-band negotiation is meaningless for the internal GPHYs: there is
+	 * no MII pinout and mt7988_setup() brings them up directly.  Let those
+	 * ports through instead of bailing out here.
+	 */
 	if (phylink_autoneg_inband(mode) &&
-	    state->interface != PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII) {
+	    state->interface != PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII &&
+	    state->interface != PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_INTERNAL) {
 		dev_err(ds->dev, "%s: in-band negotiation unsupported\n",
 			__func__);
 		return;
